  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-27 decision D-232 (notes/decisions.md): option A on #3275. Read gh issue view 3275 and DI-177. The nightly SignalReevaluationJob writes a ConditionCleared Decision Record whose sprk_privilegeflagged is copied from sprk_signal.sprk_privilegeflagged, which nothing writes (DI-64), so it always reads false. Derive it instead with the same WorkItemPrivilege rule task 225 uses at commit (DecisionCommitService.PrivilegeFlaggedAsync: WorkItemPrivilege.SourcesOf over the subject and stored sprk_evidencerefs, then FlaggedAsync), read with the job's application identity, failing closed (a read fault = flagged). Stop selecting and reading the Signal column for this. Entry points on origin/master: Services/Signals/SignalReevaluationJob.cs (the PrivilegeFlagged: line near the ConditionCleared record, ~:965, and the column select ~:1523), Services/Signals/WorkItemPrivilege.cs, DecisionCommitService.cs PrivilegeFlaggedAsync. Search by name.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF, the ontology Signal re-evaluation job.</role>
  <goal>Every ConditionCleared Decision Record carries the D-212 privilege flag derived from its Signal's subject and evidence communications, not the unwritten Signal column.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Reuse WorkItemPrivilege and, if a shared helper is cleaner than copying DecisionCommitService.PrivilegeFlaggedAsync, extract one with no behaviour change on the commit path. The flag is record accuracy only (ADR-015: never branched on). Batch the reads per pass where the job already batches; do not add per-Signal round trips that turn the nightly into N reads without bounding them (state the cost in the PR). D-145b idempotency of the ConditionCleared record must be unchanged. Run /conflict-check; read git log -5 on the files you edit.</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6 gotcha 2026-11-24">Run the relevant --filter (Signals code: "FullyQualifiedName~Signals", which includes the contract baselines; Communication: "FullyQualifiedName~Communication"; Ai: "FullyQualifiedName~Ai"); update any baseline the change moves in the same PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene when the BFF changes: publish-size delta vs a fresh master build (short paths, same zip tool, file counts) in the PR; no new HIGH CVE; no new package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11">No new service, interface, endpoint or DI registration unless the three questions are answered in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6">Filtered BFF tests only (never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests); full ArchTests (build tests/Spaarke.ArchTests explicitly first). Client code: run node scripts/quality/client-lint/client-lint.mjs check and the package jest suite.</constraint>
    <constraint source="public repo">No environment GUIDs, user or contact ids, mailbox addresses, tenant names or private access-control mechanics in code, tests, notes, commits or the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §2 / D-106">Fix only what the named issues describe. Any other defect found: report it in the task notes and to the main session; do not fix it here.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
