  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the issue(s) and entry points; record findings in notes/task-233-notes.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Failing tests first, with must-not-fire controls.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the fix.</step>
    <step order="4">Build, filtered tests, full ArchTests (BFF tasks), client checks (client tasks), publish-size delta (BFF tasks).</step>
    <step order="5">Code review and ADR check (Step 9.5); PR to master, body "Closes #3275"; notes in notes/task-233-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A test fails on origin/master: a Signal closed by condition-cleared whose evidence communication is classified Privileged (and one Potentially Privileged) yields a Decision Record with sprk_privilegeflagged = true.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Must-not-fire: evidence classified None or null gives false; the job no longer reads sprk_signal.sprk_privilegeflagged (test or guard); a read fault gives true and the closure still completes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The commit path's behaviour and tests are unchanged; D-145b idempotency test still passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build, Signals filter (contract baselines included), full ArchTests pass; publish-size delta reported.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>Deriving the flag app-only would need a new privilege or role, or would require reading communications the job does not already have access to: STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <execution>
    <protocol>Run through task-execute. Fresh branch from origin/master in a short-path worktree (C:\wt233); PR to master; do not merge (the main session reviews and merges, D-115).</protocol>
  </execution>
  <completion></completion>
